158.0,5,2.0,1.0,4.0,45,100.0,1,4.31202827371349,4.91,4.93,4.94,4.74,2131667,"The main selling point of the flat is the location - it is near lots of public transport options with shops, restaurants and cafes at the end of the street. It felt safe to walk around and was a nice ""street culture"" atmosphere. Whilst 6 people could technically sleep there, there was only one bedroom with four others needing to sleep in the main living area. The table could just fit four of us round it and the sofa wasn't very comfortable as it was also a bed. It is also in the basement so without lights was very gloomy and the lights were quite harsh. Also the coffee machine didn't work. Whilst this may sound overly  critical, it was pretty expensive for a week and we were reluctant to spend much time in the flat for these reasons.",0,0.0246,Neutral
125.0,6,2.0,1.0,4.0,29,100.0,0,4.518046062365621,4.67,4.75,4.39,4.55,960718759443282693,"Mario was the perfect host. Always responsive and helpful. His place is the perfect place to stay for your trip to Berlin! The location couldn’t be any more convenient for your stay, tram stop literally on the door step (20 second walk) and close to shops such as Lidl for your weekly shop. I wouldn’t hesitate to recommend this Airbnb and will certainly stay here again when I visit Berlin in future. Thanks Mario!",0,0.95,Positive
