139.0,2,1.0,1.0,1.0,25,96.0,1,4.279858775670925,4.8,4.82,4.89,4.66,54126149,"1. Bed room- The services were top notch. It had a big bed, almirah with a locker, a work desk, a mirror, huge windows. What else do you want? <br/>Also they had kept instant coffee in the hallway. Though I didn't try it but you surely can! <br/>2. Washroom- It was one of the best washrooms I have ever seen. Such a big one including a bath tub, amazing vibes and great lighting in room number 4. <br/>3. Host- The host was super friendly and communicated all details timely.<br/>4. Restaurants suggestions-  Vietnamese- ""Umami"", English breakfast- ""What a treat"". Both the places were at walkable distance. Burgermeister Schlesisches Tor and Duo - Sicilian Ice Cream are must try if you like burgers and gelato. Totally worth it. Also these were near the east side gallery (berlin wall) and oberbaum bridge which you would anyway visit if in berlin. <br/>5. For commuting- We took e-scooter, bus, tube. Everything was at a walkable distance. <br/>Overall, a great experience.",1,0.9939,Positive
